\begin{tcolorbox}[amberbox,height=170mm]
\sectiontitle{secondary}{Two centuries of expansion}
\BodyFont\color{textlight}
Education access has been transformed from an elite privilege into a global norm. In the early 1800s, fewer than one in five adults had any formal education. Today, more than four in five adults aged 15+ have received some primary, secondary, or tertiary schooling.
\vspace{7mm}
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1mm,y=1mm]
  \foreach \i in {0,...,9}{\draw[rounded corners=1.6mm, line width=1.2pt, draw=textmuted, fill=paperbg] (\i*22,50) rectangle ++(13,28);}
  \foreach \i in {0,1}{\draw[rounded corners=1.6mm, line width=1.2pt, draw=secondary, fill=secondary] (\i*22,50) rectangle ++(13,28);}
  \node[anchor=west] at (0,39) {\SmallFont\color{textmuted}1800: fewer than 2 of every 10 adults};
  \foreach \i in {0,...,9}{\draw[rounded corners=1.6mm, line width=1.2pt, draw=secondary, fill=secondary] (\i*22,6) rectangle ++(13,28);}
  \foreach \i in {8,9}{\draw[rounded corners=1.6mm, line width=1.2pt, draw=textmuted, fill=paperbg] (\i*22,6) rectangle ++(13,28);}
  \node[anchor=west] at (0,-5) {\SmallFont\color{textmuted}Today: more than 8 of every 10 adults};
\end{tikzpicture}
\end{tcolorbox}

\vspace{9mm}
\begin{tcolorbox}[coralbox,height=148mm]
\sectiontitle{accent}{Enrollment \(\neq\) learning}
\BodyFont\color{textlight}
School attendance is not the same as learning. In many lower-income countries, fewer than 20\% of children achieve minimum reading proficiency by the end of primary school.
\vspace{8mm}
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1mm,y=1mm]
  \fill[textmuted!28] (0,0) rectangle (208,20);
  \fill[accent] (0,0) rectangle (41.6,20);
  \draw[white, opacity=.35] (41.6,-3) -- (41.6,25);
  \node[anchor=south west] at (0,27) {\SmallFont\bfseries\color{accent}<20\% reach minimum reading proficiency};
  \node[anchor=north west] at (0,-7) {\SmallFont\color{textmuted}A learning crisis can hide behind enrollment gains.};
\end{tikzpicture}
\end{tcolorbox}

\vspace{9mm}
\begin{tcolorbox}[bluebox,height=112mm]
\sectiontitle{cyan}{Closing the gender gap}
\BodyFont\color{textlight}
Globally, gender gaps in primary and secondary enrollment have nearly closed, and young women now exceed young men in tertiary enrollment.
\vspace{5mm}
{\SmallFont\color{textmuted}\faVenus\ \faMars\ Primary and secondary: near parity globally\par\vspace{2mm}\faGraduationCap\ Tertiary: women now enroll at higher rates\par\vspace{2mm}\textcolor{accent}{Important exception:} girls remain far less likely to attend school in places such as Afghanistan.}
\end{tcolorbox}
\end{minipage}
