\begin{tcolorbox}[darkbox,height=170mm]
\sectiontitle{secondary}{A world divided by quality schooling}
\BodyFont\color{textlight}
Learning-adjusted years combine time in school with how much students actually learn. The gap is stark: children in the poorest countries receive less than one-third of the quality schooling available in wealthy nations.
\vspace{8mm}
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1mm,y=1mm]
